# Overlay for the QEMU end-to-end test (tools/e2e/run_e2e.py). The emulator has no
# W5500, I2C expander, GPIO inputs or RMT, and it does not model: QIO flash reads by the
# app (data shifted by 2 bytes) and the RS485 half-duplex UART mode (uart_wait_tx_done
# asserts) and has no Wi-Fi radio. The octal PSRAM is in sdkconfig.qemu-psram (E2E_PSRAM=1,
# issue #85); this build runs without it.
# Issue #261: as the build for the board, this build has no NVS encryption and does not check a
# signature of an OTA image. These two functions are in sdkconfig.qemu-secure (E2E_SECURE=1).
# Never flash this build.
#
# The rule for a difference between a QEMU build and the build for the board (CLAUDE.md, "QEMU-only
# code"): each option of a sdkconfig.qemu* overlay has one of these classes in its comment.
#   [hardware]    QEMU does not have this hardware: a model or another device replaces it.
#   [emulator]    A fault or a limit of QEMU: the option goes around it.
#   [test value]  The same logic as on the board with another number, so that a test is possible.
#   [variant]     A function or a diagnostic that the board build does not have, or the opposite.
#                 Only in a variant with a name and a stated reason, never in all QEMU builds.
# A class at the top of an overlay is the class of each option of that overlay.
#
# [hardware] No W5500: the OpenCores Ethernet MAC of QEMU
CONFIG_GW_ETH_OPENETH=y
# [hardware] No I2C expander, GPIO inputs or RMT (the LED): RAM models, and the shell commands
# that drive them
CONFIG_GW_IO_SIMULATED=y
# [emulator] QEMU does not model the RS485 half-duplex mode of the UART (uart_wait_tx_done asserts)
CONFIG_GW_RS485_HW_HALF_DUPLEX=n
# [variant] The default variant has no PSRAM (issue #135): it runs only the OTA trial scenarios,
# which examine logic and are faster so. sdkconfig.qemu-psram gives the PSRAM of the board back
CONFIG_SPIRAM=n
# [emulator] QEMU does not model QIO flash reads by the app (data shifted by 2 bytes)
CONFIG_ESPTOOLPY_FLASHMODE_DIO=y
# [hardware] No Wi-Fi radio. Issue #267: thus no radio as the entropy source of the RNG after
# gw_net_start; the SAR ADC source before it is the same as on the board (#126 L18, #130)
CONFIG_GW_WIFI=n
# [emulator] QEMU writes the flash image asynchronously: a reset right after the panic handler
# saved the core dump can drop its last write (the checksum) from the image. One second lets it
# land.
CONFIG_ESP_SYSTEM_PANIC_REBOOT_DELAY_SECONDS=1
# [test value] Issue #59: the E2E slow link (700 B/s through a relay) must exceed the publish budget with
# payloads of at most 6 KB once slirp's buffers are full; 2 s does, the default 8 s would not
CONFIG_GW_MQTT_PUBLISH_BUDGET_MS=2000
# [hardware] SPB-14: QEMU has no SDMMC: the store & forward spill goes to a LittleFS directory instead
CONFIG_GW_SF_SPILL_LITTLEFS=y
# [emulator] FW-1: QEMU does not model the S3 cache freeze of a flash mapping; code fetched by the other
# core while an OTA image is verified makes it abort ("Bad ram pointer"): park that core
CONFIG_GW_FW_PARK_OTHER_CORE=y
# [test value] Issue #233: the self-check confirms a new image after 30 s of uptime, not the 60 s of the board.
# QEMU runs without -icount (uptime = wall time), and the E2E waits for about 11 self-checks.
# Not less than 30 s: the E2E does actions during a trial (the other-slot button, NCMD Boot
# Other Slot, a configuration save, a panic) that need a window with PSRAM and single-threaded TCG
CONFIG_GW_FW_SELFCHECK_S=30
# [emulator] FW-1: no USB-Serial-JTAG secondary console (QEMU has no USB host anyway). Its connection
# monitor runs in every tick interrupt and reads the USB peripheral; on the core parked during
# an image verification that read faulted under QEMU's cache freeze (LoadStorePIFAddrError)
CONFIG_ESP_CONSOLE_SECONDARY_NONE=y
